<title>Worlds of Tomorrow Listings</title>
<h1>Worlds of Tomorrow</h1>

<p>
<i>Worlds of Tomorrow</i> was a digest-size magazine originated
by the Barmaray Company. It was later picked up by the Galaxy
Publishing Company as a companion to <i>Galaxy</i>. <i>Worlds of
Tomorrow</i> never had a steady publishing schedule, and was
eventually absorbed into <i>Worlds of If</i> in 1967 (also owned
by the Galaxy Publishing Company at the time). An attempt was made
to resurrect <i>Worlds of Tomorrow</i> in 1970-1971.
<p>
Thanks to Edwin M. Schaefer for the use of his collection for
the following issues: Jul65, Sep65, Jan65, Mar65, May65, and Nov65.
The rest of the data was supplied by
<a href="mailto:redacted@redacted.com">Dave Kauffman</a>.
